<article class="env-lemma" id="02K5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02K5">Lemma <span data-tag="02K5">29.35.19</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ f \ar[rd]_ p &  &  Y \ar[dl]^ q \\  &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is surjective, and smooth, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$p$ is smooth, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$q$ is locally of finite presentation<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000646519" id="a0000646519-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $q$ is smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/02JZ" data-tag="02JZ">29.26.13</a> we see that $q$ is flat. Pick a point $y \in Y$. Pick a point $x \in X$ mapping to $y$. Suppose $f$ has relative dimension $a$ at $x$ and $p$ has relative dimension $b$ at $x$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02G1" data-tag="02G1">29.35.12</a> this means that $\Omega _{X/S, x}$ is free of rank $b$ and $\Omega _{X/Y, x}$ is free of rank $a$. By the short exact sequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/02K4" data-tag="02K4">29.35.16</a> this means that $(f^*\Omega _{Y/S})_ x$ is free of rank $b - a$. By Nakayama's Lemma this implies that $\Omega _{Y/S, y}$ can be generated by $b - a$ elements. Also, by Lemma <a href="/tag/02JS" data-tag="02JS">29.29.2</a> we see that $\dim _ y(Y_ s) = b - a$. Hence we conclude that $Y \to S$ is smooth at $y$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/01V9" data-tag="01V9">29.35.14</a> part (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>